// CHAIN.QS0 - a low-entanglement chain for the MPS engine.
//
// Demonstrates: the MPS engine (--mps D), matrix-product states, and how
// low-entanglement circuits stay exact.
//
// Qubit-level explanation:
//   The circuit walks a linear chain: each step rotates one qubit (RY) and
//   couples it to the next via CNOT. Because every gate only touches
//   adjacent qubits, the entanglement across any cut stays small, so the
//   state is well represented by a matrix-product state with a modest bond
//   dimension. With D=32 the MPS engine reports zero truncation error and
//   reproduces the statevector result: the measurement histogram is
//   statistically identical to the reference engine.
//
//   This is the regime the MPS engine is designed for: it scales with
//   n*D^2 instead of 2^n, so deep low-entanglement circuits are cheap.
//
// Run:
//   plasma run examples/CHAIN.QS0 --mps 32 --shots 1000
//   plasma run examples/CHAIN.QS0 --shots 1000            (reference)
QUBITS 6
RY 0 1.3
CNOT 0 1
RY 1 0.7
CNOT 1 2
RY 2 0.7
CNOT 2 3
RY 3 0.7
CNOT 3 4
RY 4 0.7
CNOT 4 5
SHOT 1000
PRINT
END